-- title:
--   Kummer descent: p-th roots in a multi-radical extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $p$ be a prime, and let $\zeta \in K$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $n$ be a natural number, let $u : \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to K$ be a family of nonzero elements of $K$, and let $\beta : \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to L$ be elements with $\beta_i^{\,p} = u_i$ in $L$ (the image of $u_i$ under the structure map $K \to L$) for every $i$. Let $x \in K$ be nonzero and let $\gamma \in L$ satisfy $\gamma^p = x$ in $L$. Assume that $\gamma$ lies in the intermediate field $K(\beta_0, \dots, \beta_{n-1})$ of $L/K$ generated over $K$ by the range of $\beta$. Then there exist natural-number exponents $a : \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to \mathbb{N}$ and an element $w \in K$ with
--   $$x = \Bigl(\prod_{i} u_i^{\,a_i}\Bigr)\, w^{\,p}.$$
--   Thus the radicand $x$ lies in the subgroup of $K^\times$ generated by $u_0, \dots, u_{n-1}$ and the $p$-th powers, with the exponents taken nonnegative.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the Kummer correspondence in the form needed for several radicals at once: $K(x^{1/p}) \subseteq K(u_1^{1/p},\dots,u_n^{1/p})$ forces $x \in \langle u_1,\dots,u_n\rangle K^{\times p}$. It is used, together with a valuation-theoretic argument over a $p$-adic algebraic closure, to produce an element of an inertia subgroup moving a prescribed element when a valuation is not divisible by $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Field_exists_prod_pow_mul_pow_eq_of_root_mem_adjoin_roots.lean

